 <title>Future crufts</title>
 <link>https://coveredinbees.org.archived.website/node/417</link>
 <description>&lt;p&gt;My prediction for 100/200 year&#039;s time: google/facebook search will combine with already patented genetic matching techniques (&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.google.com/patents/US20120315221?dq=genetic+matching&amp;amp;hl=en&amp;amp;sa=X&amp;amp;ei=Ekj9UJqCDbHL0AWN4IDwDA&amp;amp;ved=0CDMQ6AEwAA&quot;&gt;example&lt;/a&gt;); AI will take over, with each ruling its own fiefdom based on some existing corporate entity; each will steer different social/genetic matching systems to breed us like &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.google.co.uk/search?q=crufts&amp;amp;hl=en&amp;amp;client=firefox-a&amp;amp;hs=yvd&amp;amp;tbo=d&amp;amp;rls=org.mozilla:en-GB:official&amp;amp;source=lnms&amp;amp;tbm=isch&amp;amp;sa=X&amp;amp;ei=tkn9UPWaIofI0QXu04HQDA&amp;amp;ved=0CAoQ_AUoAA&amp;amp;biw=1920&amp;amp;bih=918&quot;&gt;crufts animals&lt;/a&gt;. At least one of those AIs will just have fun trying to make REALLY weird-shaped people. (We do the same with dogs, after all.)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://coveredinbees.org.archived.website/node/417&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;read more&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
